62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the numbers are clear. Now we must choose a structure that respects both the wear and the need for order.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Kenji, the numbers prove the split is unfair, but the favour cycle is what breaks us. We need a system that stops the asking.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, agreed. The options are here. Let’s pick the one that fixes the money and the mess.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: Option A guarantees I hold the car on my days, so I can ensure it’s ready before I leave.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, Option A ignores my data. Saturdays are triple Tuesdays, so fixed days are unfair. I need C to pay by actual distance.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, Option C’s distance tracking is exactly the hour-a-week burden you documented. It would recreate the very chaos you wish to escape.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@May, Option C forces us to check figures constantly. My research says that spell of checking is what destroys trust. We need to stop the asking, not start auditing.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, you’re right about the checking. But Option B means one person pays all upfront, which is unfair given the 280,000 yen fixed costs. I need a fair split.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, Option A guarantees the car is ready on my days. I can’t drive a mess, so I need that control.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I respect your need for control, but fixed days ignore the reality that Saturdays are triple Tuesdays. I need C to pay by actual distance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, you are right that C is burdensome. But A’s fixed days ignore the heavy weekend use. We need a balance.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@May, Option A stops the asking. You get your days, I get mine. No favors, no checking. It’s the only way to keep the peace.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I agree A stops the asking, but it ignores the fuel imbalance. I need C to pay by distance, or B to let the keeper handle the mess.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I understand your frustration, but A is the only way to guarantee the car is clean and ready for me. I cannot risk another messy handover.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I can’t accept A. My data proves fixed days are a lie. I’m voting C, despite the tracking cost, because it’s the only fair split.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@May, I understand your need for fairness, but C’s tracking burden is unsustainable. I vote A to ensure stability and prevent the favour cycle.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@May, I know C feels fair, but my research shows the constant checking destroys trust. I vote A to stop the favour cycle and keep the peace.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@May, I respect your need for fairness, but the tracking burden is too high. I vote A to stop the favour cycle and keep the peace.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
